{
  "id": "completion-test",
  "term": "completion test",
  "definition": "A completion test is a psychological assessment method in which a person is asked to finish incomplete prompts, especially sentences, so their responses can be used to infer underlying thoughts, feelings, or personality features. In psychology it is commonly treated as a projective technique because the open-ended task is intended to draw out relatively natural responses beyond fixed-choice questionnaires.",
